 # The DevTools Times
 
-This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
-
+A sample news application built with Astro, React, and Tailwind CSS.
 
 ```sh
-pnpm install && pnpm run start
+pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
+pnpm dev --host 0.0.0.0 --port 11224
 ```
 
-The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
+For production, run `pnpm build` and `pnpm start` behind an HTTPS proxy.
+
+Privacy defaults: no third-party analytics, ads, remote fonts, or remote images; no credential collection. Reading lists store only explicitly saved article IDs in bounded server memory for up to 24 hours. Readers can delete them from the Privacy page. Lists may disappear after restart or eviction and do not sync across replicas.
 
-## Tech Stack
+```sh
+pnpm test:privacy
+pnpm audit:dependencies
+```
 
-- **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
-- **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
-- **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
-- **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+See [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md) for the data inventory, vendor review register, independent audit requirements, and deployment controls. Independent third-party review remains pending; automated checks are not certification.
